670 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H5/P 337 0 R/T(SENIOR CITIZENS AND PERSONS WITH DISABILITIES: You may be entitled to a property tax exemption pursuant to RCW 84.36.379 through RCW 84.36.389, or a deferral pursuant to chapter 84.38 RCW. For further information, contact the Clark County Assessor\220s Office at 564.397.2391. LIMITED INCOME: You may be entitled to a property tax deferral pursuant to RCW 84.37.030. For additional information, contact the Clark County Assessor\220s Office at 564.397.2391. LATE FEES: Past due taxes payable in 2023 and forward for residential properties with four or fewer units accrue 0.75% interest per month. All other properties accrue 1 % interest per month, and one-time penalties of 3% on June 1 and 8% on December 1. Past due taxes payable in 2022 accrue 1% interest per month, with no penalties. Past due taxes payable in 2021 and prior tax years receive 1% interest per month, and one-time penalties of 3% on June 1 and 8% on December 1 \(RCW 84.56.020\). FORECLOSURE AND PERSONAL PROPERTY DISTRAINT: Real property is subject to foreclosure when a property bill is three \(3\) years delinquent \(RCW 84.64.050\). Mobile homes are subject to distraint when a property bill is three \(3\) years delinquent \(RCW 84.56.070\). The Washington Homeownership Resource Center is available for referral to housing counseling and/or legal assistance by calling 877.894.4663. When business personal property taxes become delinquent, they are subject to immediate distraint and sale. Pursuant to RCW 84.56.090, when business personal property is sold or a change of ownership occurs, the following year\220s tax must be paid in advance at the time of sale by the seller. To assure a clean bill of sale, check with the county treasurer\220s office where the personal property is located before changing ownership of personal property. PAYMENT DATES: Property taxes are due and payable on or before April 30. If the total tax amount is $50.00 or more, the half payment indicated may be paid by April 30 with second half due on or before October 31. If property taxes are paid after the due date, the payment must include all accrued interest and penalty due at the time payment is made. A half payment, including accrued interest and penalty, may be made through October 31.)/E(SENIOR CITIZENS AND PERSONS WITH DISABILITIES: You may be entitled to a property tax exemption pursuant to RCW 84.36.379 through RCW 84.36.389, or a deferral pursuant to chapter 84.38 RCW. For further information, contact the Clark County Assessor\220s Office at 564.397.2391. LIMITED INCOME: You may be entitled to a property tax deferral pursuant to RCW 84.37.030. For additional information, contact the Clark County Assessor\220s Office at 564.397.2391. LATE FEES: Past due taxes payable in 2023 and forward for residential properties with four or fewer units accrue 0.75% interest per month. All other properties accrue 1 % interest per month, and one-time penalties of 3% on June 1 and 8% on December 1. Past due taxes payable in 2022 accrue 1% interest per month, with no penalties. Past due taxes payable in 2021 and prior tax years receive 1% interest per month, and one-time penalties of 3% on June 1 and 8% on December 1 \(RCW 84.56.020\). FORECLOSURE AND PERSONAL PROPERTY DISTRAINT: Real property is subject to foreclosure when a property bill is three \(3\) years delinquent \(RCW 84.64.050\). Mobile homes are subject to distraint when a property bill is three \(3\) years delinquent \(RCW 84.56.070\). The Washington Homeownership Resource Center is available for referral to housing counseling and/or legal assistance by calling 877.894.4663. When business personal property taxes become delinquent, they are subject to immediate distraint and sale. Pursuant to RCW 84.56.090, when business personal property is sold or a change of ownership occurs, the following year\220s tax must be paid in advance at the time of sale by the seller. To assure a clean bill of sale, check with the county treasurer\220s office where the personal property is located before changing ownership of personal property. PAYMENT DATES: Property taxes are due and payable on or before April 30. If the total tax amount is $50.00 or more, the half payment indicated may be paid by April 30 with second half due on or before October 31. If property taxes are paid after the due date, the payment must include all accrued interest and penalty due at the time payment is made. A half payment, including accrued interest and penalty, may be made through October 31.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

